.TH PBI-LINUX 1 "October 2026" "Power BI Linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pbi-linux \- community Power BI Desktop installation and launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pbi-linux
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage a dedicated per-user installation of Microsoft Power BI Desktop using
this project's versioned Wine runtime. Installing the Linux package does not
install Microsoft software. Ubuntu 24.04/26.04 and Debian 13 are experimental;
Fedora 44 remains the tested baseline. Native Wayland, a systemd user session
and a suitable Vulkan driver are required.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Download verified components and prepare Desktop after terms acceptance.
Use setup --help for local-file options.
.TP
.BI "open " [report]
Open Desktop or a PBIX, PBIP or PBIR file.
.TP
.B doctor
Check dependencies and installation integrity. Use --json for structured output.
.TP
.B profile
Show optional user-controlled resource settings; use profile --help to change them.
The Linux package does not select a resource preset.
.TP
.B update
Activate the published runtime, preserving the managed installation contract.
.TP
.B repair
Repair the existing profile in place, without a full-prefix copy or rollback.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove per-user desktop integration while preserving managed data.
The separate --purge option deletes managed installations, settings and caches.
.TP
.B connector
Inspect or install optional managed database providers; use connector --help.
.SH FILES
User state follows XDG data, config, cache and state directories.
Package removal does not delete these user files.
.SH NOTES
Microsoft does not support this community installation. Keep report backups.
Repair and update modify the existing installation without snapshots.
An interruption or failure can require repair or reinstallation; no automatic
rollback is available. The legacy rollback command reports that it is unavailable.
A successful diagnostic does not certify all reports or connectors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pbi-linux " --help"
and /usr/share/powerbi-linux/docs/user/debian-ubuntu.md.
